lese cuisine","cuisine/senegalese-cuisine",[["Yassa (food)","dish/yassa-food"]]],["Singaporean Chinese cuisine","cuisine/singaporean-cuisine-chinese-inspired",[["Satay","dish/satay"]]],["Singaporean cuisine","cuisine/singaporean-cuisine",[["Satay","dish/satay"]]],["South African cuisine","cuisine/south-african-cuisine",[["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"]]],["Soviet cuisine","cuisine/soviet-cuisine",[["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"]]],["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",[["Pottage","dish/pottage"]]],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia",[["Steckerlfisch","dish/steckerlfisch"]]],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",[["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"]]],["Yoruba cuisine","cuisine/yoruba-cuisine",[["Draw soup","dish/draw-soup"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Palm oil","ingredient/palm-oil"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Offal","ingredient/offal"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Crayfish","ingredient/crayfish"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Red onion","ingredient/red-onion"]]}]},"ingredient/nutmeg":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/nutmeg","n":"Nutmeg","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 9 dishes across 7 cuisines","intro":[["Nutmeg is the seed, or the ground spice derived from the seed, of several tree species of the genus Myristica; fragrant nutmeg or true nutmeg (M. fragrans) is a dark-leaved evergreen tree cultivated for two spices derived from its fruit: nutmeg, from its seed, and mace, from the seed covering. It is also a commercial source of nutmeg essential oil and nutmeg butter. The Banda Islands, in Maluku, Indonesia, are the main producer of nutmeg and mace, and the true nutmeg tree is native to the islands."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-nutmeg"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutmeg"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":7,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Nasi gandul","dish/nasi-gandul"],["Semur (Indonesian stew)","dish/semur-indonesian-stew"],["Sop saudara","dish/sop-saudara"]]],["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Banbury cake","dish/banbury-cake"],["Potted shrimps","dish/potted-shrimps"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Pumpkin pie","dish/pumpkin-pie"]]],["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine",[["Pepernoot","dish/pepernoot"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Passatelli","dish/passatelli"]]],["Javanese cuisine","cuisine/javanese-cuisine",[["Nasi gandul","dish/nasi-gandul"]]],["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",[["Salchichón","dish/salchichon"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Nutmeg, mace, cardamoms, raw","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":189054,"top":[["Guatemala","cuisine/guatemalan-cuisine",72323],["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",50006],["Indonesia","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",40315],["Laos","cuisine/lao-cuisine",8842],["Nepal","cuisine/nepalese-cuisine",8806],["Sri Lanka","cuisine/sri-lankan-cuisine",4209],["Bhutan","cuisine/bhutanese-cuisine",1540],["Tanzania","cuisine/tanzanian-cuisine",816],["Grenada","cuisine/culture-of-grenada-cuisine",622],["Honduras","cuisine/honduran-cuisine",584],["Trinidad and Tobago","cuisine/trinidad-and-tobago-cuisine",321],["Ethiopia","cuisine/ethiopian-cuisine",161],["Papua New Guinea","cuisine/papua-new-guinean-cuisine",112],["Malawi","cuisine/malawian-cuisine",91],["Malaysia","cuisine/malaysian-cuisine",81]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cinnamon","ingredient/cinnamon"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Sweet soy sauce","ingredient/sweet-soy-sauce"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Cloves","ingredient/cloves"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"],["Zante currant","ingredient/zante-currant"],["Zest","ingredient/zest"],["Caraway seed","ingredient/caraway-seed"]]}]},"ingredient/cassava":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/cassava","n":"Cassava","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 9 dishes across 11 cuisines","intro":[["A starchy root that came out of South America. ",["Taíno","cuisine/taino-heritage-foodways"]," descendants and ",["Garifuna","cuisine/garifuna-foodways"]," women grate and dry it for ",["Casabe","dish/casabe"],", ",["Kichwa","cuisine/amazonian-kichwa-foodways"]," women ferment it into ",["Chicha","dish/chicha"],", and the ",["Guaraní","cuisine/guarani-foodways"]," relied on it as much as on corn. In Paraguay it is baked into ",["chipa","dish/chipa"],"."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"UNESCO, Traditional knowledge and practices for the making and consumption of cassava bread","url":"https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/traditional-knowledge-and-practices-for-the-making-and-consumption-of-cassava-bread-02118"},{"name":"Sounds and Colours, Chicha, an ancestral beverage to feed body and soul","url":"https://soundsandcolours.com/articles/ecuador/chicha-an-ancestral-beverage-to-feed-body-and-soul-7430/"},{"name":"Gastronomica, Making chipas in Paraguay","url":"https://gastronomica.org/2009/05/04/making-chipas-paraguay/"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-cassava"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cassava"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":11,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Getuk goreng","dish/getuk-goreng"],["Oncom","dish/oncom"